From b549b827765498e7365e6a6029d88106a8bcc972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:40:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): quarantine round 4: per-host notice, acceptance
 in the catch-up txn, withhold-order replay [daveey]

Review of #3796 at b2ff1715:
1. Owner-notice key is containment-quarantine:<board>:<receipt>:<gateway>:<first-seen ms> (quarantine rows
   now carry quarantined_at), so two hosts file two cards and a re-quarantine after a release files again.
2. The acceptance row is written inside the catch-up apply transaction (with certification and the lift), from
   evidence prefetched before it; a failed catch-up leaves no acceptance and every hold.
3. A freed protected event whose evidence no longer certifies is quarantined under its own receipt during the
   release (kind identity_changed/event_differs, or uncertifiable); its card is filed and the CLI names it.
4. Withheld rows carry a withhold epoch; replay order is (epoch, seq), so snapshot rows (seq 0) withheld during
   a resync replay after the feed rows withheld before it.
5. Non-primary live file: the lift could leave a picked-up copy claimable until the next repair; it now applies
   the replica's current certified rows of each freed task (adopt_receipts, the pickup path) in the lift
   transaction, and refuses while the replica still holds the task.
6. reconcile withholds rows of held tasks instead of restoring them.
7. install() refuses any other column set of an existing containment_sync_* table (QuarantineSchemaRefused, a
   ContainmentRefused, so only that board's round ends); an example survey found none on the checked gateways.
   Downgrade behaviour documented in the module docstring.
8. release_board turns an apply-time sqlite3.Error/RuntimeError into exit 1 with the holds kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
